# What the MCP image does NOT need.
#
# `.git` IS NOT HERE AND MUST NOT BE. It is a RUNTIME dependency: the toolkit's FTS cache key
# is `git rev-parse HEAD` plus a hash of `git status --porcelain`, and corpus_overview()
# shells out to `git log -1`. Exclude it and repo_state() collapses to a constant, so content
# changes stop invalidating the index — silently, with everything still reporting healthy.

# THE SNAPSHOTS ARE A CI ARTIFACT, NOT A RUNTIME ONE. 3,335 committed .txt extractions,
# 149 MB, and the server never opens them: `verify-provenance` re-slices every `## Full text`
# against them in CI, which is where they matter. The documents themselves carry the text the
# server serves.
#
# VERIFIED RATHER THAN ASSUMED, because "nothing reads it" is exactly the claim that is wrong
# once and expensively — federal-reference excluded its snapshots and its citation module
# turned out to read one AT IMPORT, so the framework raised FileNotFoundError before serving
# a request. Checked here by moving the directory away and exercising the server:
#
#   ensure_index      ok            (builds from counties/*.md, not snapshots)
#   resolve_citation  ors-215.203   direct hit into the sibling corpus
#   resolve_citation  ors-197a.350  the renumbering redirect still works
#   search_corpus     3 hits
#   corpus_overview   ok
#   get_document      body: 13,342 chars — the full text is in the document, not the snapshot
#
# This corpus declares no snapshot_slice_module and no tools_module, and its citation module
# reads `_meta/ors-dispositions.yml` only, so there is no import-time path into this directory.
# Re-run the check above if any of that changes.
_meta/snapshots/

# The raw sources are already gitignored, so a shallow-clone build never sees them. Named
# anyway: the documented build is `git clone --depth 1 && docker build`, but someone will
# eventually build from a working tree, and there 4.3 GB of PDFs would land in the image.
_meta/snapshots/*.pdf
_meta/snapshots/*.html
_meta/snapshots/*.xml
_meta/snapshots/*.json

# Rebuilt on demand inside the image by the Dockerfile's ensure_index step. Copying a
# host-built index in would ship one keyed to the host's repo state.
_meta/.cache/

# Never inputs to the server.
.github/
.obsidian/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
